<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><BaseHead title="PBR Shader Study — Source & Setup" description="Shader source, Unity setup, references, and art dependencies for the PBR Shader Study." /></head>
  <body><ProjectHeader /><main>
    <a href="/projects/pbr-shader">← Back to the project</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">UNITY PBR SHADER STUDY</p><h1>Source &amp; setup</h1>
    <p>Two shader files from the implementation shown in the case study. These downloads contain shader source; models, textures, the HDR environment, and a configured Unity scene are separate dependencies.</p>
    <section><h2>Shader files</h2><ul><li><a href="/projects/pbr-shader/source/PBR_simple.shader" download>PBR_simple.shader ↓</a> — direct lighting, simple ambient, and emission.</li><li><a href="/projects/pbr-shader/source/PBR_IBL.shader" download>PBR_IBL.shader ↓</a> — direct lighting plus SH/lightmaps and reflection-probe sampling.</li></ul></section>
    <section><h2>Run in Unity</h2><ol><li>Use Unity 2022.3.36f1 with the Built-in Render Pipeline and Linear color space.</li><li>Import the shader files into an Assets/Shaders folder. Create a material and select PBR_IBL or PBR_Simple in its Shader menu.</li><li>Assign albedo and a normal map. The Metallic Map uses R for metallic and Alpha for smoothness; Smoothness defaults to 0.75. AO uses the Occlusion texture’s G channel.</li><li>Add a directional light. For PBR_IBL, configure an HDR skybox and update environment lighting; add and bake a Reflection Probe for local reflections. SH/lightmap data is supplied by Unity.</li><li>For a Standard comparison, use the same model, camera, lighting, texture inputs, and smoothness scaling. Disable Standard’s Height Map to match the custom shader’s inputs.</li></ol><p>These shaders target opaque ForwardBase shading. Compiling and rendering in your local Unity project is required; the website build does not validate Unity shader compilation.</p></section>
    <section><h2>References</h2><p>LearnOpenGL — PBR: <a href="https://learnopengl.com/PBR/Theory">Theory</a>, <a href="https://learnopengl.com/PBR/Lighting">Lighting</a>, <a href="https://learnopengl.com/PBR/IBL/Diffuse-irradiance">Diffuse irradiance</a>, and <a href="https://learnopengl.com/PBR/IBL/Specular-IBL">Specular IBL</a>.</p><p>Unity 2022.3 documentation: <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/2022.3/Documentation/Manual/LightProbes.html">Light Probes</a>, <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/2022.3/Documentation/Manual/ReflectionProbes.html">Reflection Probes</a>, and <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/2022.3/Documentation/Manual/Lightmappers.html">Lightmappers</a>.</p><ul><li>Unity 2022.3 Built-in source: UnityStandardBRDF.cginc and UnityGlobalIllumination.cginc.</li></ul></section>
    <section><h2>External art dependencies</h2><ul><li>Models and textures: <a href="https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/3d/props/clothing/armor/pbr-corinthian-helmets-230928">PBR Corinthian Helmets</a> by Ferocious Industries, via Unity Asset Store.</li><li>HDR environment: <a href="https://polyhaven.com/a/mirrored_hall">Mirrored Hall</a> by Grzegorz Wronkowski, via Poly Haven (CC0).</li></ul></section>
  </main><ProjectFooter /></body>
